[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TyreClass" load_steps=2 format=3]

; Factors as responses (dry x factor) over the all-season tyre; brackets are docs/sources.md. dry 1.10: an SUV-size test put the best all-season 6.5 m (18 %) behind the summer reference's 37.0 m [70]; car sizes run closer (estimate). Snow 0.55 in all: 0.47 of the Winter class's, between AutoBild's ABS stops from fifty, the summer reference at 0.40 of the winter's friction (55.3 against 22.3 m [66]) and at 0.56 (1.8x the winters' stops [215]); VTI's peak on packed snow, 0.26 braking against a winter's 0.40 [214], is a brush-model fit, not a stop. Ice 0.74 in all: 35.5 m against 26.2 from 40 km/h [71]. Field, grass and mud factors 0.9: fewer voids (estimate). crr: label B against the all-season's C, 2020/740 [74].

